   "subject": "mirt solution depents on item order",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\" align=\"left\" style=\"line-height:normal\">Hey Phil,<u></u><u></u></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" align=\"left\" style=\"line-height:normal\">using your package I became aware of some odd behavior of\nthe mirt-function.<u></u><u></u></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" align=\"left\" style=\"line-height:normal\">By coincidence I realized that the results change depending\non the order of items within the data set.<u></u><u></u></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" align=\"left\" style=\"line-height:normal\">Here is a simple example of what I mean: <u></u><u></u></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" align=\"left\" style=\"line-height:normal\">data &lt;- expand.table(LSAT7)<u></u><u></u></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" align=\"left\" style=\"line-height:normal\">mod1 &lt;- mirt(data,2)<u></u><u></u></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" align=\"left\" style=\"line-height:normal\">mod2 &lt;- mirt(data[2,4,3,1,5],2)<u></u><u></u></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" align=\"left\" style=\"line-height:normal\">However, mod1 and mod 2 are not equivalent. How can this be?<u></u><u></u></p>\n\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" align=\"left\" style=\"line-height:normal\">Regards,</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" align=\"left\" style=\"line-height:normal\">Kornelius</p></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
